{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואני ידעתי", :translit "v'ani yadati", :gloss "And I know"} {:he "נ' עקומה", :translit "n akumah", :gloss "fifty gnomic form"} {:he "חמשים מכות", :translit "chamishim makot", :gloss "fifty plagues"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "נ'", :b "חמשים"}], :frame {:text "The midrash counts that the Egyptians were struck with fifty plagues in total: during the year the plagues were in Egypt the Egyptians suffered ten plagues, and at the sea they received an equivalent measure multiplied further. The enumeration of fifty plagues appears in the liturgical framework of the haggadah expounding 'the hand of God' as five-fold, which itself derives from Exodus 3:19 where the verse 'And I know' introduces the punishment.", :sources ["Exodus 3:19" "Mechilta Beshalach 7" "Mishnah Eduyot 2:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "להלך", :translit "lelechet", :gloss "to go"} {:he "כי מאן ה' לתתי להלך עמכם", :translit "ki ma'ein Hashem latet lelechet imchem", :gloss "for the LORD refused to let me go with you"} {:he "יודע אני כי לא יתן אתכם להלך", :translit "yodeia ani ki lo yiten etchem lelechet", :gloss "I know that he will not let you go to walk"} {:he "מאן ה' לתתי להלך עמכם", :translit "ma'ein Hashem latet lelechet imchem", :gloss "the LORD refused to let me go with you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["להלך" "כי מאן ה' לתתי להלך עמכם"]}], :frame {:text "When Pharaoh sought counsel on how to deal with Israel, three great figures served as his advisors: Jethro, Job, and Balaam. Jethro objected and fled; Job remained silent; Balaam advised persecution. This tradition is recorded in Bavli Sotah 11a. Balaam's opposition to Israel is demonstrated in Numbers 22:13–14, where Balak's messengers report back that 'the LORD refused to let me go with you,' and Balaam continues his campaign to curse the nation (Numbers 22–24).", :sources ["Bavli Sotah 11a" "Numbers 22:13" "Numbers 22:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "נ'